{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1020363-what-makes-pugmire-different","id":1020363,"title":"What makes Pugmire different?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Realms of Pugmire"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-21T06:56:45-08:00","id":1020363,"title":"What makes Pugmire different?","content":"Are there any mechanics that cause Pugmire to standout? Mechanically it looks rather 5e D&amp;D, so what makes the game different from just 5e where we say everyone is a dog?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T09:39:36-08:00","id":1020444,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of mechanics under the hood that are distinct. Some obvious examples:<br /> <br /> 1) No experience points. Character go up in level after a significant adventure.<br /> 2) No equipment rules. Weight is ignored, and characters are assumed to have whatever equipment makes sense for them. They can even make a saving throw to 'remember' equipment.<br /> 3) Evolving abilities. Instead of getting a specific power at each level, characters can choose to pick a new power (called a &quot;trick&quot;) or refine existing powers to make them more effective.<br /> 4) Level cap at 10.<br /> 5) Fortune. Characters earn a currency called fortune that anyone in the group can use for rerolling.<br /> <br /> You can check out a slightly older version of the rules for just $2, if you like! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/172260/Pugmire-Early-Access\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/...e-Early-Access</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}